zenghuaqing.translation:
In the Brocade City, strings and pipes sound day after day, drifting thick;
Half of it enters the river wind, half enters the clouds.
This music should belong only to Heaven;
In the human world, how many times can one hear it?

niaomingjian.translation:
With the man at ease, osmanthus blossoms fall;
The night is still, the spring mountain empty.
The moon comes out and startles the mountain birds;
Now and then they call in the spring stream.

dengkehou.translation:
The old days of being cramped and wretched are not worth boasting of;
Today I am free and carefree, my thoughts without limit.
In the spring wind, pleased with myself, my horse's hooves fly;
In one day I have seen all the flowers of Chang'an.

chishang.translation:
Soft and gentle, the cool wind stirs;
bleak and chill, the cold dew falls.
The orchids fade, their flowers only now turning white;
the lotus leaves are torn, yet still green.
Alone it stands, a crane roosting on the sandbank;
two by two they fly, fireflies lighting the water.
Such a lonely, desolate scene
meets me just as I am sobering from my wine.

yuweng.translation:
The old fisherman moors at night by the western cliff;
at dawn he draws clear Xiang water and burns bamboo of Chu.
The mist clears, the sun rises, and no one can be seen;
one creak of the oar, and hills and waters turn green.
Looking back, the boat has gone down the middle of the stream,
and over the cliff the carefree clouds chase one another.
